#!grafli v2
# Bookmarks & Flows demo
# Open the Flows tab in the side panel (\ toggles the panel) and play a
# flow, or press F5 to present one fullscreen. Capture your own viewpoints
# with gb (logical) or gB (exact viewport); gf records a new flow.

@ box client "Client" -20,0 160x80 %primary
@ box api "API Gateway" 280,0 180x80 %secondary
@ box auth "Auth Service" 280,160 180x80 %soft
@ box svc "Order Service" 560,0 180x80 %tertiary
@ box db "Postgres" 560,160 180x80 %muted
@ box cache "Redis" 860,0 160x80 %subtle

@ arrow client -> api "request"
@ arrow api -> auth "verify token"
@ arrow api -> svc "route"
@ arrow svc -> db "read/write"
@ arrow svc -> cache "cache reads"
@ arrow auth -> db "user lookup"

@ note n1 280,280 "Every request is authenticated before it is routed."

@ bookmark bm_overview "The whole system" @client,api,auth,svc,db,cache ~pad=80 "Six services: a request enters at the client and fans out across the gateway, auth, orders, and storage."
@ bookmark bm_entry "Entry point" @client,api "Requests arrive at the API Gateway, the single front door."
@ bookmark bm_auth "Authentication" @api,auth "Before routing, the gateway verifies the token against the Auth Service."
@ bookmark bm_data "Data layer" @svc,db,cache "The Order Service reads and writes Postgres, caching hot reads in Redis."

@ flow tour "Architecture tour" bm_overview bm_entry:6 bm_auth:6 bm1 bm_data:8 "Start wide, then walk a request from the front door through auth into the data layer."
@ flow security "Security path" bm_entry:5 bm_auth:6 bm_data:5 "Follow a request through authentication into the data it can reach."
@ bookmark bm1 "" @cache
@ note n2 -80,360 """
md:
## Pair grafli with your AI

grafli isn't just a diagram editor — it's the canvas your coding agent
uses to communicate complex systems back to you. The bundled **grafli
skill** teaches the agent how to produce idiomatic `.grafli` files —
proper layouts, semantic edge labels, code-mode notes for
review-oriented diagrams, plus a "plan before you write" loop that
keeps the output focused and readable.

Extract the skill from your installed copy and point your agent at it:


| AI tool | Where the skill goes | Docs |
|---------|---------------------|------|
| Claude Code | `~/.claude/skills/grafli/SKILL.md` | <https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills> |
| OpenCode | `~/.config/opencode/skills/grafli/SKILL.md` | <https://opencode.ai/docs/skills> |
| Codex CLI | append to `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` | <https://agents.md/> |
""" ~width=95
@ note n3 799,439 "Some other note ...\n\nBut with longer text so we can evaluate things and more." ~width=32
@ box box1 "A Node" 1012,237 160x80
@ box box2 "A Node" 1325,235 160x80
@ box box3 "A Node" 1631,232 160x80
@ box box4 "A Node" 1645,516 160x80
@ arrow box1 -> box2
@ arrow box2 -> box3
@ arrow box3 -> box4
@ bookmark bm2 "A Node" @box1 ~iso
@ bookmark bm3 "A Node" @box2 ~iso
@ bookmark bm4 "A Node" @box3 ~iso
@ bookmark bm5 "A Node" @box4 ~iso
